course: dictionary
lesson: 2788
title: Like and dislike
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word dislike is the opposite of like. To dislike means not to like someone or something. A dislike is the feeling itself, so you can have a dislike of cold porridge.
explain: Read this: «Most cats dislike water, but tigers are happy swimmers.» The word but is a clue. It shows that tigers are different from most cats, so dislike means that most cats do not like water.
explain: Dislike can be a verb, as in «I dislike spiders», or a noun, as in «Spiders are one of my biggest dislikes». Look at the words around it to see which one you have.
fact: Dislike means not to like someone or something.
fact: A dislike is a feeling of not liking something.
fact: «Take a dislike to» means to start not liking someone.
fact: Online, a «dislike» is a button you press to show you don't like a post.
fact: «Likes and dislikes» means the things you enjoy and the things you do not enjoy.
exercise: «Most cats dislike water.» What does dislike mean here? | *Do not like | Forget about | Swim in | Love very much
exercise: In «Spiders are one of my biggest dislikes», what kind of word is dislikes? | A verb, an action word | *A noun, a naming word for a feeling | A joke | A question word
exercise: Lily says, «I dislike the cold.» Which word means the same as dislike? | Love | Forget | Enjoy | *Not like
test: When Sam was rude, Ben began to take a dislike to him. What does take a dislike to mean? | *Start to not like | Lose a bet against | Give a present to | Forget the name of
test: Which sentence uses dislike as a noun? | *Rainy days are one of my dislikes. | Please dislike the rain. | We disliked the film. | I dislike rainy days.
exam: In «Most cats dislike water, but tigers are happy swimmers», which word is a clue that tigers are different? | water | *but | swimmers | Most
